<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $40.2 mln Feb 12.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $40.2 mln Feb 12.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $40.2 million surplus on Feb 12 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 12</p>
<p>Exports: $51.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $64.3 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $145.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $93.1 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $40.2 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.044 million</p>
<p>Imports: $862 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.267 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.014 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $435 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off. -- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418</p>
